Turn Vulkan defragmentation off unless SDL_GPU_VULKAN_DEFRAGMENT asks for it.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    Defragmentation moves live textures, and some come out holding other contents.
    Anatomy's seven-tile skin bake in headless Studio drew corrupt tiles in 4 of 40
    runs with it on and 0 of 60 with it off; the CPU inputs and the graph signatures
    were identical in good and bad runs. The cause inside it is not known: allowing
    it only while no other command buffer was being recorded still gave 2 of 60.

COST
    Freed ranges inside a partly used allocation are reused but not compacted, so a
    fragmented heap holds more memory.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Pinned SDL commit: fa2c02bb6e21974a89ea9824bc53c9932abe5f9c.
    Re-point the start of VULKAN_INTERNAL_DefragmentMemory. Remove this patch once
    the corruption is found. Applies with private queues on or off. Do not edit the
    SDL submodule.

--- a/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
+++ b/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
@@ -11202,6 +11202,12 @@ static bool VULKAN_INTERNAL_DefragmentMemory(
     VulkanRenderer *renderer,
     VulkanCommandBuffer *commandBuffer)
 {
+    // Off: moving live textures corrupts some of them. See the patch's header.
+    (void)commandBuffer;
+    if (!SDL_GetHintBoolean("SDL_GPU_VULKAN_DEFRAGMENT", false)) {
+        return true;
+    }
+
     renderer->defragInProgress = 1;
     commandBuffer->isDefrag = 1;
 
